7,1444,1445],{},"credentials: 'include'"," as well.",[242,1448,1450],{"id":1449},"how-oidc-works-with-your-application","How OIDC Works with Your Application",[1452,1453,1454,1457,1460,1463],"ol",{},[250,1455,1456],{},"Your platform administrator enables one or more OIDC configurations for your application (e.g., Google, Microsoft)",[250,1458,1459],{},"Your UI looks the user up by email at its API host; for a user of an identity provider the answer carries the provider's authorization URL, and the UI sends the browser there",[250,1461,1462],{},"The provider returns the browser to the API host, which validates the provider's response, looks the user up in your application, and sets the session cookie",[250,1464,1465,1466,1469,1470,1473,1474,1478,1479,1482],{},"The browser returns to ",[267,1467,1468],{},"\u002F"," on the site that started the sign-in, which connects with the session; a sign-in that fails returns instead to the ",[267,1471,1472],{},"\u002Flogin"," page of your application's ",[272,1475,1477],{"href":1476},"\u002Fapps\u002Fapplication-structure\u002Fapplications-and-projects#applications","primary UI"," with an ",[267,1480,1481],{},"error"," parameter",[242,1484,1486],{"id":1485},"reusable-providers","Reusable Providers",[238,1488,1489,1490,1492,1493,1496],{},"Kinotic OS registers once with providers like Google and Microsoft. The platform operator provisions these as ",[267,1491,269],{}," entities; your organization admin enables them for your application by adding the configuration id to your application's ",[267,1494,1495],{},"oidcConfigurationIds",". End users see \"Kinotic OS\" on the consent screen, and your application benefits without any provider registration.",[238,1498,1499,1500,1502,1503,1505],{},"The same ",[267,1501,269],{}," shape is used for an organization's enterprise SSO (e.g. a corporate Okta instance) — see ",[272,1504,167],{"href":168}," for how the platform-vs-org distinction is captured by reference rather than by a flag on the entity.",[234,1507,1509],{"id":1508},"user-management","User Management",[238,1511,1512,1513,1516,1517,1520],{},"Application-scope users are ",[253,1514,1515],{},"pre-created"," by an administrator before they can authenticate. This is a deliberate security design — having a valid Google account does not automatically grant access to your application. Self-service signup applies to the ",[272,1518,1519],{"href":163},"Organization scope"," (the admin who runs the org); the same data model supports application-scope self-signup, but enabling it is admin-controlled.",[238,1522,1523,1524,1527],{},"Your organization administrator manages your application's users from the organization's ",[253,1525,1526],{},"Members"," page:",[247,1529,1530,1536],{},[250,1531,1532,1535],{},[253,1533,1534],{},"Local users"," are created with an email and password",[250,1537,1538,1541],{},[253,1539,1540],{},"OIDC users"," are created with an email only — the OIDC subject is linked automatically on first login",[238,1543,1544,1545,1547],{},"For details on user and OIDC configuration management, see the ",[272,1546,162],{"href":163}," platform guide.",[1549,1550,1551],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .s7zQu, html code.shiki .s7zQu{--shiki-light:#39ADB5;--shiki-light-font-style:italic;--shiki-default:#89DDFF;--shiki-default-font-style:italic;--shiki-dark:#89DDFF;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic}html pre.shiki code .sMK4o, html code.shiki .sMK4o{--shiki-light:#39ADB5;--shiki-default:#89DDFF;--shiki-dark:#89DDFF}html pre.shiki code .sTEyZ, html code.shiki .sTEyZ{--shiki-light:#90A4AE;--shiki-default:#EEFFFF;--shiki-dark:#BABED8}html pre.shiki code .sfazB, html code.shiki .sfazB{--shiki-light:#91B859;--shiki-default:#C3E88D;--shiki-dark:#C3E88D}html pre.shiki code .s2Zo4, html code.shiki .s2Zo4{--shiki-light:#6182B8;--shiki-default:#82AAFF;--shiki-dark:#82AAFF}html pre.shiki code .swJcz, html code.shiki .swJcz{--shiki-light:#E53935;--shiki-default:#F07178;--shiki-dark:#F07178}html .light .shiki span